WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.025 --> 00:00:16.888
The next morning Ally walked into town to shop for parts.

2
00:00:18.228 --> 00:00:20.789
It had taken only two hours to train Flo yesterday.

3
00:00:21.269 --> 00:00:25.130
The new waitress had learned the job so quickly, it was as if she'd been working at Ray's

4
00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:30.191
forever. As Ally walked along, she stopped and looked around.

5
00:00:30.211 --> 00:00:33.464
"I'm going to miss it here," she thought.

6
00:00:33.484 --> 00:00:40.027
"And I need to remember everything so I can tell my parents about Earth.

7
00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:45.709
After all, I am the first Astralian to make contact with Earthlings."

8
00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:50.591
Ally began daydreaming about the elaborate welcome she'd receive when she returned home.

9
00:00:50.611 --> 00:00:55.573
"Mom and Dad will be so proud of me," she said.

10
00:00:55.593 --> 00:00:58.655
"I bet the elder council will give me a medal!"

11
00:00:58.675 --> 00:01:00.555
"A medal for what?"

12
00:01:00.936 --> 00:01:01.496
someone asked.

13
00:01:02.236 --> 00:01:04.978
Ally snapped out of her daydream to see Kate standing in front of her.

14
00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:08.059
"Oh, uh nothing!"

15
00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.140
Ally said quickly.

16
00:01:14.163 --> 00:01:16.304
like to get a medal one day," Kate said.

17
00:01:16.324 --> 00:01:20.086
"Can you get one for having fantastic taste in fashion?"

18
00:01:22.347 --> 00:01:22.928
Ally laughed.

19
00:01:22.948 --> 00:01:24.028
"I don't know.

20
00:01:25.049 --> 00:01:26.229
But you deserve one!"

21
00:01:26.249 --> 00:01:29.651
"How come you're not working today?"

22
00:01:30.032 --> 00:01:30.612
Kate asked.

23
00:01:31.596 --> 00:01:33.737
"I have the morning off," Ally explained.

24
00:01:33.757 --> 00:01:35.658
"I have some shopping to do."

25
00:01:35.678 --> 00:01:38.499
"Ooh!" Kate said.

26
00:01:38.519 --> 00:01:40.280
"I'll come with you!"

27
00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:42.781
Ally gulped.

28
00:01:43.121 --> 00:01:47.142
She liked Kate a lot, but there was no way Kate could join this shopping expedition.

29
00:01:47.162 --> 00:01:55.726
"I'd really love that, but, um, I'm not shopping for anything exciting, just some, you know—" "Oh, boring

30
00:01:55.786 --> 00:01:57.567
things, like shampoo and soap?"

31
00:01:57.947 --> 00:01:58.487
Kate asked.

32
00:01:58.507 --> 00:02:06.213
"Exactly." "How about if we go shopping tomorrow after your work shift?"

33
00:02:06.513 --> 00:02:07.073
Kate asked.

34
00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:09.474
"I know the cutest dress shop!

35
00:02:09.514 --> 00:02:10.274
You'll love it.

36
00:02:10.834 --> 00:02:11.615
See you tomorrow!"

37
00:02:12.755 --> 00:02:14.815
Ally waved as she started toward the museum again.

38
00:02:14.836 --> 00:02:18.757
"Shopping with Kate sounds fun," she thought.

39
00:02:18.777 --> 00:02:21.017
"And I do have some extra money.

40
00:02:21.677 --> 00:02:26.079
I'd love to buy a new dress and wear it to my birthday party, when I finally get

41
00:02:26.119 --> 00:02:26.659
back home.

42
00:02:27.079 --> 00:02:30.140
I'll wow all my friends with unique Earth fashion!"

43
00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:39.463
The Sandville UFO Museum was a tall glass building with banners displaying planets and stars.

44
00:02:40.884 --> 00:02:43.586
As soon as Ally stepped through the door, an alarm blared.

45
00:02:45.047 --> 00:02:46.448
"Ahh!" She jumped back.

46
00:02:46.468 --> 00:02:47.708
"What did I do?"

47
00:02:48.369 --> 00:02:51.271
Phil, who worked as a security guard at the museum, hurried over.

48
00:02:51.291 --> 00:02:54.332
"These dang metal detectors!"

49
00:02:54.953 --> 00:02:56.454
He sighed and turned the alarm off.

50
00:02:56.474 --> 00:02:59.716
"You can come on in, Ally.

51
00:03:00.192 --> 00:03:04.936
We just installed these alarms for the sci-fi convention, and they go off at the littlest thing.

52
00:03:05.376 --> 00:03:06.517
I need to adjust them again."

53
00:03:07.598 --> 00:03:11.881
Phil held the door open for Ally, and she entered the main hall, which was filled with models

54
00:03:11.921 --> 00:03:12.521
of spaceships.

55
00:03:16.284 --> 00:03:18.766
silly things aren't usually here either," Phil said.

56
00:03:18.786 --> 00:03:21.908
"The convention organizers bring them in every year."

57
00:03:23.509 --> 00:03:24.750
Ally squinted at the models.

58
00:03:25.331 --> 00:03:26.912
She'd never seen ships like these before.

59
00:03:29.016 --> 00:03:30.177
"They're not very realistic."

60
00:03:30.197 --> 00:03:32.940
"You're telling me."

61
00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:34.621
Phil rolled his eyes.

62
00:03:34.641 --> 00:03:36.683
"Well, enjoy the museum.

63
00:03:37.023 --> 00:03:38.304
I need to fix these alarms."

64
00:03:41.147 --> 00:03:44.930
Ally was tempted to look around at some of the exhibits, but she reminded herself that she didn't

65
00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:45.631
have much time.

66
00:03:45.991 --> 00:03:49.054
She had to get the parts and then get to the diner for work by noon.

67
00:03:50.996 --> 00:03:53.117
She hurried into the gift shop and found a sales clerk.

68
00:03:55.019 --> 00:03:55.640
"Excuse me.

69
00:03:56.044 --> 00:04:01.146
Can you tell me where I can find fuel cells, beta-booster coils, and other spaceship parts?"

70
00:04:02.387 --> 00:04:04.248
"Ha-ha," the clerk said.

71
00:04:05.428 --> 00:04:06.089
Ally frowned.

72
00:04:06.109 --> 00:04:07.529
"What's so funny?"

73
00:04:07.549 --> 00:04:11.211
"Listen, kid, the convention hasn't started yet.

74
00:04:12.131 --> 00:04:15.693
Until it does, spare me the wacko sci-fi talk, okay?"

75
00:04:15.713 --> 00:04:19.595
"But I really need these parts," Ally said.

76
00:04:19.615 --> 00:04:22.516
"I'm sure you do," the clerk said.

77
00:04:23.064 --> 00:04:26.686
"But like I've told a million other people, we don't sell that kind of stuff here.

78
00:04:27.206 --> 00:04:29.407
You should go to Everything Mart, like everyone else."

79
00:04:29.427 --> 00:04:32.568
"Thanks," Ally said.

80
00:04:33.649 --> 00:04:35.589
She turned around, trying to decide what to do.

81
00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:40.151
Going to Everything Mart seemed like the only option; she didn't have any other ideas about where to

82
00:04:40.191 --> 00:04:43.493
shop. "I still have plenty of time," she thought.

83
00:04:43.513 --> 00:04:46.394
"As long as—" "Ally!"

84
00:04:47.034 --> 00:04:48.195
Dr. Lloyd hurried over.

85
00:04:48.215 --> 00:04:50.556
"I'm glad I ran into you!

86
00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:54.703
I want to invite you to the opening of my exhibit on Friday, the first day of the

87
00:04:54.743 --> 00:05:00.729
convention." "I'd love to come," Ally said politely, even though she knew she'd be zooming through outer space

88
00:05:00.789 --> 00:05:01.109
by then.

89
00:05:01.129 --> 00:05:04.252
"It's going to be so exciting," Dr.

90
00:05:04.292 --> 00:05:04.772
Lloyd said.

91
00:05:04.792 --> 00:05:12.719
"I'll be unveiling proof that extraterrestrial life-forms not only exist, but also He paused to look around before

92
00:05:12.779 --> 00:05:13.659
leaning in close to her.

93
00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:18.604
"They are here among us—closer than anyone thinks.

94
00:05:19.189 --> 00:05:21.374
And we have to be prepared to fight them off!"
